So he handpicked his own crew before he quit.

00:17:16.775 --> 00:17:19.515
Since we've found their base, let's just go in and wipe them out.

00:17:19.945 --> 00:17:21.085
We can't yet.

00:17:21.385 --> 00:17:22.715
Why not? What's the problem?

00:17:23.255 --> 00:17:25.155
If we just get rid of them right now,

00:17:25.485 --> 00:17:27.525
we won't be able to do anything about...

00:17:27.685 --> 00:17:28.695
all their criminal franchises overseas.

00:17:29.525 --> 00:17:32.665
But we don't even know where those overseas franchises are.

00:17:32.725 --> 00:17:33.995
How are we supposed to track them all down?

00:17:34.165 --> 00:17:36.035
Writer Go creates crime scenarios...

00:17:36.065 --> 00:17:37.765
and distributes them to all the franchises.

00:17:38.135 --> 00:17:42.235
That means this island is connected to a global criminal network.

00:17:42.835 --> 00:17:46.645
But to handle that kind of volume, they'd need a dedicated server.

00:17:46.845 --> 00:17:47.845
And that server...

00:17:48.645 --> 00:17:50.975
is most likely hidden somewhere around here.

00:17:53.245 --> 00:17:56.685
- Hey. - Gosh! You scared me!

00:17:59.725 --> 00:18:02.125
It's just me. Reporter Bong.

00:18:02.695 --> 00:18:04.125
Do you have to sneak up on us like that?

00:18:04.255 --> 00:18:07.225
Can't you just show up normally? Like you're clocking in for work.

00:18:07.265 --> 00:18:08.895
Sorry, force of habit.

00:18:10.395 --> 00:18:11.405
There we go.

00:18:11.805 --> 00:18:14.735
But squatting for so long, doesn't it hurt your knees?

00:18:15.175 --> 00:18:16.175
I'm fine.

00:18:17.675 --> 00:18:20.305
I'm okay because I have this. It's good for your joints.

00:18:20.705 --> 00:18:22.245
- Gosh, this is... - Hey, isn't that from...

00:18:22.915 --> 00:18:23.915
It looks familiar.

00:18:26.285 --> 00:18:28.615
- So, what did you need? - Right.

00:18:29.085 --> 00:18:31.354
I overheard you guys talking.

00:18:31.355 --> 00:18:33.625
I thought maybe this could help.

00:18:38.095 --> 00:18:39.095
Okay, guys.

00:18:39.725 --> 00:18:40.725
Let's move it there.

00:18:42.335 --> 00:18:43.365
Go on.

00:18:45.305 --> 00:18:47.335
Those are servers and cooling equipment.

00:18:47.635 --> 00:18:51.345
To bypass a dedicated server, I'll need my own equipment.

00:18:51.475 --> 00:18:53.005
It's back at the office.

00:18:53.545 --> 00:18:55.945
- I'll go get it in the morning. - Okay.

00:18:56.015 --> 00:18:57.875
Driver Kim, can you hold out until then?

00:19:00.815 --> 00:19:03.185
Go on. I'll find a way to stall them.

00:19:03.755 --> 00:19:06.555
How? Those jerks will kill anyone on a whim.

00:19:09.055 --> 00:19:10.155
So what?

00:19:11.155 --> 00:19:12.325
We'll just do some killing of our own.

00:19:13.525 --> 00:19:15.265
Hey, killing them sounds good.

00:19:15.535 --> 00:19:18.135
- Who should we kill first? - Who first? We're killing them all.

00:19:18.205 --> 00:19:20.165
- Let's go all out. - Right.

00:19:20.435 --> 00:19:22.635
So, what's the order? We kill this one, then that one?

00:19:22.705 --> 00:19:24.675
- Yes, that works. - Can I be next?

00:19:24.945 --> 00:19:26.905
Oh, no. Let's just go by age.

00:19:26.975 --> 00:19:28.815
- Oh, so I guess I'm up first. - Yes.

00:19:28.875 --> 00:19:31.615
- Who's up after me? - That'd be me. Let's do that.

00:19:38.555 --> 00:19:40.655
- We're going to get rich off this. - Yes.

00:19:49.635 --> 00:19:51.295
The presentation is over,

00:19:52.035 --> 00:19:54.635
but I still don't see any money on the table.

00:19:54.875 --> 00:19:58.245
As I mentioned, our guy went to get the money.

00:19:58.905 --> 00:19:59.905
Right.

00:20:00.575 --> 00:20:02.475
I saw him leave on the boat.

00:20:03.815 --> 00:20:08.015
Why don't you start deciding which business you'd like to open?

00:20:08.955 --> 00:20:10.955
So what you're suggesting, Writer Go,

00:20:11.885 --> 00:20:15.555
is we start with ping for two years to learn the ropes and get set up,

00:20:15.625 --> 00:20:17.455
then switch to the site model? Is that it?

00:20:18.195 --> 00:20:19.195
That's right.

00:20:19.825 --> 00:20:24.265
I'll continue to send you scripts for new profitable plans quarterly.

00:20:24.835 --> 00:20:25.835
And one more thing.

00:20:26.165 --> 00:20:30.305
Since it got a little messy earlier, I'll take ten percent off...

00:20:30.935 --> 00:20:31.945
your monthly subscription fee.

00:20:34.075 --> 00:20:35.145
This is hilarious.

00:20:35.775 --> 00:20:39.285
It's like a chicken franchise where you pay royalties to corporate...

00:20:39.345 --> 00:20:42.355
- and sends you their secret sauce. - You're right.

00:20:43.285 --> 00:20:44.585
It's pretty similar.

00:20:45.325 --> 00:20:47.825
So, to ensure your future business is successful,

00:20:48.625 --> 00:20:51.925
we'll do our best to help.

00:20:52.195 --> 00:20:53.865
All right then, we will...

00:20:54.365 --> 00:20:56.235
trust the expert...

00:20:56.595 --> 00:20:58.265
- and go with ping. - Wait a minute!

00:20:59.535 --> 00:21:02.175
No, wait. We have the manpower,

00:21:02.405 --> 00:21:05.045
and if we just push a little harder, can't we go right to the site?

00:21:05.475 --> 00:21:08.945
And from the pitch, it sounds like the cost difference isn't huge.

00:21:09.245 --> 00:21:12.945
Sir, instead of doing too much from the start,

00:21:14.445 --> 00:21:18.015
- build a solid base first, then... - Come on.

00:21:18.355 --> 00:21:20.624
Come on. "A solid base"?

00:21:20.625 --> 00:21:22.025
For us, if you get caught, it's over.

00:21:22.055 --> 00:21:25.895
- Then let's go all in. Right? - Exactly.

00:21:25.965 --> 00:21:30.165
It's about building a solid base, but we also need to save capital,

00:21:30.365 --> 00:21:34.065
so we can upgrade the site later. I've explained all this already,

00:21:34.205 --> 00:21:36.175
so why act like this is new to you? What do you want from me?

00:21:36.235 --> 00:21:37.375
No.

00:21:37.735 --> 00:21:41.345
I say we go straight for the site. I don't have much time left.

00:21:41.405 --> 00:21:43.415
I can't afford to waste time like this.

00:21:43.915 --> 00:21:46.885
You all came here because I said so, didn't you? Right?

00:21:46.945 --> 00:21:50.715
- So just do what I say. - Says who? It's my money!

00:21:50.785 --> 00:21:55.155
Then why not split the capital and do both at the same time?

00:21:55.455 --> 00:21:57.455
If we do both, at least one is bound to succeed.

00:21:57.595 --> 00:21:59.025
Don't be ridiculous!

00:21:59.525 --> 00:22:00.995
You're new, so just stay out of it.

00:22:01.165 --> 00:22:03.935
Stay out of it? I can't believe this guy.

00:22:04.065 --> 00:22:07.505
Old man, just because I'm quiet, do you think I'm a pushover?

00:22:07.565 --> 00:22:08.575
Did you just call me an old man?

00:22:08.705 --> 00:22:11.945
With that ridiculous hair, you're getting an attitude with me?

00:22:12.075 --> 00:22:13.075
Hey!

00:22:13.975 --> 00:22:15.175
You'll startle the Buddha.

00:22:16.275 --> 00:22:17.675
You people have no respect.

00:22:18.115 --> 00:22:19.145
Monk.

00:22:20.645 --> 00:22:25.285
I think we'll need a moment to talk amongst ourselves.

00:22:25.425 --> 00:22:26.425
Right.

00:22:26.925 --> 00:22:28.895
I just finished setting up the barbecue.

00:22:29.225 --> 00:22:30.755
Guess I'll have to feed it to the dogs.

00:22:31.055 --> 00:22:32.065
Darn these guys.

00:22:32.165 --> 00:22:35.435
I was wondering what that smell was. So it was the barbecue.

00:22:35.865 --> 00:22:37.665
Perfect, I was starving anyway.

00:22:37.735 --> 00:22:39.935
Since the fire's already going, let's eat first and talk later.

00:22:40.005 --> 00:22:43.835
We're all in this together, right? Yes, let's go.

00:22:43.905 --> 00:22:46.405
You got an extra pair of gloves? I'm a master at the grill.

00:22:46.505 --> 00:22:50.075
- I love meat! Meat! - Gosh, my hip is killing me.

00:22:57.285 --> 00:22:59.355
- Here, eat up. - Here, honey.

00:22:59.425 --> 00:23:00.755
Having a barbecue at a temple.

00:23:01.895 --> 00:23:04.225
- You too. - Gosh, it's delicious.

00:23:04.455 --> 00:23:05.925
It's really good.

00:23:08.895 --> 00:23:11.195
To think they were mortal enemies just a while ago.

00:23:11.935 --> 00:23:13.265
Call me when the job comes up.

00:23:17.375 --> 00:23:18.375
Aren't you having any?

00:23:19.175 --> 00:23:22.675
- I'm fine. Please eat up. - This meat is incredible.

00:23:24.315 --> 00:23:25.315
By the way,

00:23:25.915 --> 00:23:28.415
there's something to take care of before we start the business.

00:23:31.315 --> 00:23:33.325
The taxi company CEO who came with me...

00:23:33.785 --> 00:23:34.785
I want him taken care of.

00:23:35.555 --> 00:23:38.125
- Pardon? - You saw what happened earlier.

00:23:39.095 --> 00:23:42.865
He's not the boss, but he acts like it and expects special treatment.

00:23:43.465 --> 00:23:44.565
It's really getting on my nerves.

00:23:49.075 --> 00:23:51.705
I did all the research and put this whole plan together.

00:23:52.475 --> 00:23:54.505
All he needs to do is put his money in and take his cut.

00:23:55.045 --> 00:23:57.245
But he still thinks he's the boss. That jerk.

00:23:57.715 --> 00:23:59.185
So you're asking me to...

00:23:59.915 --> 00:24:01.415
That guy... Boss Choi?

00:24:01.715 --> 00:24:03.685
He seemed terrifyingly good at his job.

00:24:05.385 --> 00:24:07.285
I'll make it worth his while,

00:24:07.655 --> 00:24:08.695
so let's get him on it.

00:24:23.835 --> 00:24:27.745
Gosh, this Maitreya Buddha looks ancient.

00:24:27.975 --> 00:24:29.715
It looks like it's over 500 years old.

00:24:30.215 --> 00:24:31.685
I doubt you wanted to know the Buddha's age...

00:24:32.615 --> 00:24:34.785
when you asked to speak with me in private.

00:24:35.955 --> 00:24:38.185
What was it you urgently needed to discuss?

00:24:39.625 --> 00:24:42.555
Since you put it that way,

00:24:42.625 --> 00:24:45.295
I'll get straight to the point.

00:24:46.665 --> 00:24:49.395
I've been holding my tongue for a long time,

00:24:50.135 --> 00:24:51.635
but I just can't take it anymore.

00:24:53.905 --> 00:24:57.175
I'm older than him,

00:24:57.535 --> 00:25:00.005
it's my money, and I'm the CEO,

00:25:00.505 --> 00:25:02.915
but from the way he acts, you'd think he was the boss.

00:25:03.645 --> 00:25:05.645
When all he did was drive us here.

00:25:08.615 --> 00:25:11.785
Here's what I'm getting at, Monk.

00:25:12.625 --> 00:25:15.995
I need you to take care of that taxi driver who came with me.

00:25:17.125 --> 00:25:19.995
I'll make sure you're handsomely rewarded.

00:25:20.425 --> 00:25:22.894
What's this all of a sudden?

00:25:22.895 --> 00:25:25.365
I mean, once the tour is over,

00:25:25.435 --> 00:25:28.165
isn't it only natural for the guide to disappear?

00:25:29.005 --> 00:25:30.005
Right?

00:25:31.405 --> 00:25:32.605
That's it.

00:25:33.375 --> 00:25:34.605
His face...

00:25:36.315 --> 00:25:38.385
- Blessed be the Goddess of Mercy. - His face...

00:25:43.415 --> 00:25:45.355
Can I have a word with you?

00:25:46.855 --> 00:25:51.325
After listening, I realized we don't need this many people.

00:25:51.655 --> 00:25:54.625
The money comes to me first.

00:25:56.295 --> 00:25:57.295
Except for me,

00:25:59.605 --> 00:26:01.065
can't you kill everyone else?

00:26:03.375 --> 00:26:06.145
It's easier to deal with one person than a group,

00:26:06.205 --> 00:26:08.145
and it'll make getting the job done smoother, right?

00:26:09.445 --> 00:26:10.945
I'll even pay you extra.

00:26:11.745 --> 00:26:12.745
Even Kim Do Gi?

00:26:13.185 --> 00:26:16.955
- Yes. - I thought you two were a thing.

00:26:21.755 --> 00:26:22.955
What a nice day.

00:26:26.165 --> 00:26:27.295
Finally.

00:26:27.995 --> 00:26:28.995
Fi...

00:26:29.795 --> 00:26:30.795
Finally?

00:26:31.735 --> 00:26:33.465
Throw that jerk into the ocean.

00:26:34.865 --> 00:26:36.475
Drop him somewhere deep,

00:26:38.005 --> 00:26:39.445
so no one will ever find him.

00:26:44.345 --> 00:26:45.915
Does that make me a bad person?

00:26:47.485 --> 00:26:48.485
What...

00:26:49.255 --> 00:26:50.485
What are you saying?

00:26:51.785 --> 00:26:54.025
Make sure you kill him.

00:26:58.865 --> 00:26:59.865
Honey.

00:27:01.095 --> 00:27:03.065
- Honey. - Honey!

00:27:04.435 --> 00:27:07.365
Honey, I brought your favorite meat.

00:27:08.475 --> 00:27:10.274
- This is just... - I think it's spoiled.

00:27:10.275 --> 00:27:12.075
A complete madhouse.

00:27:18.045 --> 00:27:19.715
Driver Kim, in your opinion,

00:27:20.085 --> 00:27:21.885
who do you think they'll listen to out of all of us?

00:27:23.055 --> 00:27:24.055
I wonder.

00:27:24.115 --> 00:27:27.185
They'll likely listen to me, right? I'm the boss, after all.

00:27:28.655 --> 00:27:31.555
I have a feeling they'll listen to Driver Kim.

00:27:31.755 --> 00:27:33.725
He and Writer Go seemed to be on the same page.

00:27:34.865 --> 00:27:37.295
I have a feeling they'll listen to Go Eun.

00:27:37.765 --> 00:27:40.135
It's easier to deal with one person, right?

00:27:40.665 --> 00:27:42.875
What's their deal? Those losers.

00:27:42.975 --> 00:27:45.675
It doesn't look like they even want to hire us.

00:27:45.745 --> 00:27:47.445
Then what's with them asking us to kill each other?

00:27:48.405 --> 00:27:51.985
If they don't intend on hiring us, why did they come out here?

00:27:52.185 --> 00:27:54.145
I'm not curious enough to...

00:27:54.845 --> 00:27:56.285
finding that out.

00:27:56.485 --> 00:27:58.724
Go Eun told them to kill all of us!

00:27:58.725 --> 00:28:00.555
What if those guys...

00:28:00.585 --> 00:28:02.025
decide to listen to her right this second?

00:28:02.295 --> 00:28:04.025
Shouldn't we be coming up with a plan right now?

00:28:05.195 --> 00:28:07.325
How long have we been on this island?

00:28:07.565 --> 00:28:09.735
About six or seven years?

00:28:11.065 --> 00:28:12.765
It's about time we moved.

00:28:14.335 --> 00:28:16.075
Let's start packing our things.

00:28:16.475 --> 00:28:19.005
This time, let's find somewhere with a little more charm...

00:28:19.505 --> 00:28:22.075
and a nice atmosphere.

00:28:23.775 --> 00:28:26.985
Are the workers coming with us or are we hiring new ones?

00:28:27.085 --> 00:28:29.185
We'll be traveling as light as possible.

00:28:29.485 --> 00:28:30.485
Right.

00:28:32.755 --> 00:28:33.855
Writer Go.

00:28:34.585 --> 00:28:35.995
Since we're moving anyway,

00:28:37.095 --> 00:28:40.625
why don't we set up near a church? I think I'm...

00:28:41.165 --> 00:28:43.194
Amitabha Buddha

00:28:43.195 --> 00:28:44.665
I'm more cut out to be a pastor.

00:28:44.895 --> 00:28:46.465
Knock yourself out.

00:28:47.265 --> 00:28:48.575
What about renewing Lee Gi Hyeon's contract?

00:28:49.075 --> 00:28:52.905
- We already took all his money. - I sent my men to take care of him.

00:28:54.205 --> 00:28:57.475
That's why we get paid upfront, isn't it?

00:28:57.545 --> 00:29:00.015
Right. What about the people from the taxi company?

00:29:00.345 --> 00:29:01.545
Once they bring the money,

00:29:02.515 --> 00:29:03.755
we'll take care of them right away.

00:29:17.295 --> 00:29:19.205
(Samheung Inn)

00:29:20.335 --> 00:29:22.805
There are too many eyes on us here,

00:29:22.935 --> 00:29:26.505
let's meet at Reporter Bong's shack later.

00:29:27.075 --> 00:29:28.205
I have to check on something first.

00:29:30.515 --> 00:29:31.515
Okay.

00:30:16.595 --> 00:30:17.595
Yes?

00:30:19.525 --> 00:30:21.225
The boat should be arriving any minute now,

00:30:22.135 --> 00:30:23.465
so let's get the meeting started.

00:30:24.365 --> 00:30:26.165
The sooner we get this over with, the better.

00:30:26.735 --> 00:30:29.905
I was waiting. And it sounds like the boat's arriving right on time.

00:30:31.435 --> 00:30:32.905
I'll see you shortly.

00:31:12.445 --> 00:31:15.455
- I think Go Eun was right. - What are you talking about?

00:31:16.015 --> 00:31:17.185
Lee Gi Hyeon is dead.

00:31:18.285 --> 00:31:19.955
What? They took the money and just killed him?

00:31:20.185 --> 00:31:22.925
As soon as Chief Park gets back, I think they'll get rid of us too.

00:31:23.625 --> 00:31:25.095
How much time do you think you need?

00:31:25.565 --> 00:31:27.825
Even if I find the server room on the first try,

00:31:28.265 --> 00:31:31.235
if they have multi-layered security, it'll be at least 30 to 40 minutes.

00:31:32.305 --> 00:31:35.135
- Thirty to forty minutes. - And that's if I'm lucky.

00:31:35.575 --> 00:31:36.575
And one more thing.

00:31:37.005 --> 00:31:38.475
Samheung Temple has to be empty.

00:31:51.785 --> 00:31:53.225
Driver Kim, what are you doing?

00:31:53.885 --> 00:31:54.885
How does it look?

00:31:55.655 --> 00:31:58.295
- Doesn't it look like a cash bag? - Wait.

00:31:58.395 --> 00:32:00.265
- Give me a hand with this. - Sure.

00:32:05.935 --> 00:32:07.135
Yes, Writer Go.

00:32:07.865 --> 00:32:09.075
The thing is,

00:32:09.475 --> 00:32:13.775
I was hoping we could talk, just us, before the main meeting.

00:32:15.245 --> 00:32:16.245
Right.

00:32:17.875 --> 00:32:19.685
Okay, I'll head over there right now.

00:32:21.245 --> 00:32:23.685
What's going on? You can't leave without telling me the plan.

00:32:23.755 --> 00:32:26.385
There is no plan. Until Go Eun finishes her work,

00:32:26.525 --> 00:32:29.295
we all just have to stall for time as best we can.

00:32:30.055 --> 00:32:31.055
Hey...

00:32:31.725 --> 00:32:32.725
What?

00:32:41.835 --> 00:32:43.235
Hey, Monk. It's me.

00:32:43.905 --> 00:32:47.305
I was hoping we could talk privately before the meeting.

00:32:48.005 --> 00:32:49.475
Somewhere private.

00:32:49.875 --> 00:32:52.285
Okay, let's meet at the gukbap place right now.

00:32:55.855 --> 00:32:57.855
Gosh, if everyone just takes off, what am I supposed to do?

00:32:58.855 --> 00:33:01.625
Gosh, how am I supposed to stall for time? Goodness.

00:33:03.195 --> 00:33:04.795
Okay, let's do this.

00:33:12.865 --> 00:33:14.035
The boat's already here,

00:33:14.735 --> 00:33:16.905
so why were you in such a hurry to see me?

00:33:16.975 --> 00:33:18.535
Get in. We can talk on the way.

00:33:21.575 --> 00:33:23.814
It's the bag, isn't it?

00:33:23.815 --> 00:33:26.045
Goodness. Come on, get in.

00:33:26.315 --> 00:33:27.315
I'll put it in the back for you.

00:33:27.885 --> 00:33:28.885
Gosh.

00:33:31.885 --> 00:33:32.885
All right, then.

00:33:41.225 --> 00:33:43.295
I'll ensure a safe ride.

00:33:47.335 --> 00:33:50.975
Gosh, the gukbap is here. Thank you so much.

00:33:51.035 --> 00:33:52.035
Here, let me get that.

00:33:52.605 --> 00:33:55.245
- Is your name A Na? - Yes. And you are?

00:33:55.715 --> 00:33:57.645
I'm Jang Seong Cheol.

00:34:00.815 --> 00:34:02.585
I'll go on up and get things ready for the meeting.

00:34:04.785 --> 00:34:08.185
(Samheung Gukbap)

00:34:09.095 --> 00:34:11.155
This is a very serious matter.

00:34:11.355 --> 00:34:13.925
Is there a problem?

00:34:14.725 --> 00:34:16.895
Take a look. This here...

00:34:17.565 --> 00:34:20.535
This is a Busan pork and rice soup, with boiled pork.

00:34:20.605 --> 00:34:21.805
You see the clear broth?

00:34:22.735 --> 00:34:24.375
But look, there are sesame seeds in it.

00:34:25.135 --> 00:34:27.145
And sesame seeds are a hallmark of the Naju style, are they not?

00:34:27.375 --> 00:34:30.215
I have to say, it's quite a perplexing combination.

00:34:30.415 --> 00:34:33.515
I see. You must have one of those food blogs.

00:34:33.585 --> 00:34:36.485
- A blog? No, certainly not. - Perhaps it's time...

00:34:37.555 --> 00:34:39.025
you get to the point.

00:34:39.755 --> 00:34:42.025
What was it you needed to discuss so urgently?

00:34:42.625 --> 00:34:44.595
- Monk. - Yes.

00:34:44.825 --> 00:34:46.665
Either way, I have the money.

00:34:46.765 --> 00:34:48.265
There's no need to rush.

00:34:49.865 --> 00:34:51.795
What I wanted to say was...

00:34:52.035 --> 00:34:53.205
Wait, what's this?

00:34:54.065 --> 00:34:55.335
Not wheat noodles,

00:34:56.205 --> 00:34:57.875
but buckwheat noodles?

00:34:59.445 --> 00:35:01.075
This is the Gangwon Province style.

00:35:03.015 --> 00:35:04.945
Is A Na from Gangneung?

00:35:05.715 --> 00:35:06.915
Is her family from Gangneung?

00:35:08.015 --> 00:35:09.015
Is she?

00:35:11.755 --> 00:35:12.855
Ma'am!

00:35:24.535 --> 00:35:26.635
Hey, we've got plenty of time left.

00:35:27.035 --> 00:35:30.175
Let's kill some time, just us. I heard that back in Apgujeong...

00:35:30.235 --> 00:35:32.035
I need to go there and get ready.

00:35:32.175 --> 00:35:34.775
All the money's here anyway. What's the rush?

00:35:34.845 --> 00:35:38.245
Man, I even got the small bills. This thing weighs a ton.

00:35:38.715 --> 00:35:40.645
This should be enough for the pot, right?

00:35:41.015 --> 00:35:42.615
Not that it matters, since I'm going to win it all anyway.

00:35:45.485 --> 00:35:48.755
- Isn't that company money? - So? I'll win and put it back.

00:35:48.855 --> 00:35:50.195
So what should we play? Go-Stop?

00:35:52.025 --> 00:35:54.265
What are you going to do if you lose it all?

00:35:55.635 --> 00:35:57.635
If you lose, are you going to bet an arm or something?

00:35:57.935 --> 00:36:00.605
Why is this thing still attached?

00:36:00.865 --> 00:36:03.305
I can't even hold a woman's hand. Might as well cut it off.

00:36:17.015 --> 00:36:21.425
- Seotda. How about it? - Seotda? Okay!

00:37:08.405 --> 00:37:09.505
Am I in the wrong place?

00:37:13.475 --> 00:37:14.705
So, when are you going to bring it up?

00:37:17.975 --> 00:37:20.015
That urgent matter you wanted to discuss.

00:37:22.955 --> 00:37:24.015
Right.

00:37:24.355 --> 00:37:27.525
You still haven't decided on my proposal, have you?

00:37:28.185 --> 00:37:29.225
Right, not yet.

00:37:30.855 --> 00:37:34.065
Actually, I had a few drinks with the CEO,

00:37:34.125 --> 00:37:35.965
and we had a real heart-to-heart.

00:37:37.265 --> 00:37:38.765
I think we can spare him.

00:37:39.935 --> 00:37:43.575
Seriously? You called me here in such a rush just for that?

00:37:44.335 --> 00:37:46.575
Hey, what could be more urgent than this?

00:37:48.405 --> 00:37:49.445
All right, fine.

00:37:50.315 --> 00:37:52.915
Let's go back up. Looks like you brought the money anyway.

00:37:54.485 --> 00:37:57.785
Then kill the accountant instead.

00:37:58.855 --> 00:38:00.355
I've decided she has to die.

00:38:01.425 --> 00:38:04.055
She's getting prettier every day. I can't have that.

00:38:05.225 --> 00:38:06.695
She'll definitely cheat on me.

00:38:10.335 --> 00:38:12.635
You're a real handful, you know that?

00:38:18.305 --> 00:38:19.305
A handful?

00:38:22.545 --> 00:38:24.175
This is good to have when you're tired.

00:38:25.845 --> 00:38:26.845
Want some?

00:38:28.215 --> 00:38:29.215
It's really delicious.

00:38:36.255 --> 00:38:37.255
Delicious.

00:38:38.325 --> 00:38:39.325
Well?

00:39:50.595 --> 00:39:52.265
Look at these jerks.

00:40:14.355 --> 00:40:17.095
Gosh, how many layers of security did they put up?

00:40:17.755 --> 00:40:19.155
So paranoid.

00:40:25.735 --> 00:40:26.764
Gap, Oh.

00:40:26.765 --> 00:40:28.165
(Gap, Oh: March, June)

00:40:28.405 --> 00:40:29.504
Hey, it's Dok, Sa.

00:40:29.505 --> 00:40:31.675
(Dok, Sa: January, April)

00:40:31.735 --> 00:40:32.745
Al, Li.

00:40:32.805 --> 00:40:34.475
(Al, Li: January, February)

00:40:35.075 --> 00:40:39.785
That must sting. I'll make you all some spicy soup later.

00:40:40.815 --> 00:40:42.085
You're pretty good.

00:40:42.755 --> 00:40:45.715
Man, Seotda looks easy, but it's actually pretty tough.

00:41:02.205 --> 00:41:05.405
- Hey, what gives? - It's time to get to work.

00:41:06.175 --> 00:41:10.245
Hey, you can't just win and run. That's just bad form.

00:41:10.415 --> 00:41:13.515
If you really have to go, good form means you leave the money.

00:41:14.245 --> 00:41:15.515
Why would I leave my own money?

00:41:16.315 --> 00:41:17.855
Because it was my money to begin with.

00:41:19.285 --> 00:41:23.125
Hey, we haven't even gotten a call. They'll call if they need us.

00:41:23.225 --> 00:41:24.325
Come on.

00:41:26.065 --> 00:41:27.965
At least clean us out before you leave.

00:41:28.365 --> 00:41:29.435
Then we'll call it fair.

00:41:34.035 --> 00:41:36.935
Fine. Let's all go all-in for the final round.

00:41:37.335 --> 00:41:38.375
I'm in.

00:41:38.705 --> 00:41:41.175
Okay, last hand's over and we're starting a new game,

00:41:41.505 --> 00:41:42.845
so I'll be the one to deal, right?

00:41:43.615 --> 00:41:45.245
- Deal. - All right.

00:41:45.945 --> 00:41:48.285
Abracadabra.

00:41:57.195 --> 00:41:59.025
(Firewall bypass 1: Failed)

00:42:04.635 --> 00:42:05.635
(Firewall bypass 2: Failed)

00:42:05.635 --> 00:42:06.635
(3rd failure triggers server shutdown.)

00:42:17.175 --> 00:42:18.945
(Firewall bypass successful)

00:42:25.055 --> 00:42:28.625
And as a little bonus, the premium database.

00:42:29.255 --> 00:42:30.325
Go!

00:42:31.155 --> 00:42:34.095
Honey. It's me. Where are you?

00:42:34.495 --> 00:42:37.135
Hey, honey. I'm driving right now.

00:42:37.465 --> 00:42:40.465
- Are you done with work? - Yes.

00:42:40.965 --> 00:42:45.205
- I miss you so much. - You do?

00:42:45.705 --> 00:42:47.505
Oh, my gosh, that's crazy.

00:42:47.875 --> 00:42:49.545
I was just thinking I missed you too.

00:42:49.815 --> 00:42:51.245
We're totally on the same wavelength.

00:42:51.815 --> 00:42:56.555
- Then come see me. You will, right? - Of course I will.

00:42:57.155 --> 00:43:00.085
Honey, I'm coming as soon as I can. Just wait for me.

00:43:00.525 --> 00:43:01.885
Okay.

00:43:02.285 --> 00:43:05.025
- I love you, honey. - I love you more!

00:43:11.065 --> 00:43:12.805
Darn it. Seriously.

00:43:13.365 --> 00:43:14.365
Get out.

00:43:14.735 --> 00:43:17.075
- What? - You heard her. She misses me.

00:43:19.375 --> 00:43:21.505
You're telling me to get out? Here?

00:43:22.345 --> 00:43:25.875
We can finish our conversation after I get back.

00:43:26.415 --> 00:43:27.415
Finish what?

00:43:28.745 --> 00:43:30.055
What is there to finish?

00:43:31.315 --> 00:43:32.985
We've been driving around until sunset.

00:43:33.825 --> 00:43:36.155
We haven't said a single word to each other!

00:43:36.795 --> 00:43:39.625
What? Do you want to see my girlfriend too?

00:43:42.595 --> 00:43:43.735
Unbelievable...

00:43:44.165 --> 00:43:45.165
Go.

00:43:48.505 --> 00:43:50.505
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:43:57.445 --> 00:44:00.715
That jerk! Who's he dealing with? Does he have any idea who I am?

00:44:01.845 --> 00:44:02.885
Where am I?

00:44:04.455 --> 00:44:08.625
In Andong, there's Jungang Market. It used to be an old cattle market.

00:44:08.785 --> 00:44:12.595
In the market's center, they add scallions, oxblood, cabbage,

00:44:12.795 --> 00:44:16.465
and simmer them into this rich, hearty stew.

00:44:16.595 --> 00:44:19.835
The gukbap there is amazing. The line is always incredibly long.

00:44:20.435 --> 00:44:22.205
But this gukbap...

00:44:22.265 --> 00:44:25.605
is made with a rich, slow-brewed beef bone broth.

00:44:26.005 --> 00:44:30.375
But speaking of bone broth, try the Uiryeong bean sprout gukbap.

00:44:30.775 --> 00:44:34.315
- That stuff is on another level. - Excuse me a moment, Mr. Jang.

00:44:35.785 --> 00:44:38.355
Forgive me for saying this,

00:44:39.285 --> 00:44:42.425
but I have walking and bowel issues, and intermittent claudication.

00:44:42.485 --> 00:44:45.355
I suffer from spinal stenosis that can cause these issues.

00:44:45.425 --> 00:44:49.995
I can't sit still for long. So, could you stop talking about soup,

00:44:50.935 --> 00:44:52.195
and get to the point?

00:44:52.265 --> 00:44:54.165
What? Monk, I thought you liked gukbap.

00:44:54.835 --> 00:44:58.005
Based on your face, you look like a total soup fanatic.

00:44:58.235 --> 00:45:02.745
This information is highly prized among soup connoisseurs, Monk.

00:45:02.805 --> 00:45:05.315
Your knack for reading faces has really gotten rusty.

00:45:05.675 --> 00:45:10.085
So please, just get to the point. My back is really starting to hurt.

00:45:10.885 --> 00:45:12.485
And now my ears are starting to hurt too.

00:45:12.885 --> 00:45:14.355
So please, just get on with it.

00:45:15.025 --> 00:45:16.725
(An Go Eun: Done)

00:45:16.795 --> 00:45:18.025
Yes, my apologies.

00:45:19.025 --> 00:45:20.565
- The thing is... - Yes.

00:45:21.125 --> 00:45:24.865
Since I'll probably be asking you for many favors in the future, Monk,

00:45:25.265 --> 00:45:28.005
I prepared a small gift of my appreciation.

00:45:30.275 --> 00:45:31.775
A gift?

00:45:32.135 --> 00:45:33.475
Yes.

00:45:37.515 --> 00:45:38.575
Ta-da!

00:45:39.585 --> 00:45:41.615
It's roasted seaweed. The delicious kind.

00:45:43.485 --> 00:45:44.515
Here, look.

00:45:45.115 --> 00:45:47.885
You see this seaweed? You just tear it open like this.

00:45:48.725 --> 00:45:49.725
See?

00:45:50.095 --> 00:45:53.025
Wrap it around a bite of rice like this,

00:45:54.525 --> 00:45:56.935
and then you eat it.

00:45:57.335 --> 00:45:59.435
It's not too salty, and it's so savory.

00:45:59.805 --> 00:46:02.235
It's got a clean taste. Absolutely amazing.

00:46:04.635 --> 00:46:06.305
Gosh, is that it?

00:46:07.575 --> 00:46:09.005
You came all this way just to give me seaweed?

00:46:09.875 --> 00:46:12.045
And not even a whole box, just a single pack.

00:46:12.345 --> 00:46:15.785
If you don't want the seaweed, I guess I'll just have it myself.

00:46:16.085 --> 00:46:17.615
Anyway, I'll get to my point in due time.

00:46:17.685 --> 00:46:18.685
Is he trying to make me curse?

00:46:18.755 --> 00:46:21.885
Gosh. They say you're supposed to talk less as you get older.

00:46:21.955 --> 00:46:23.025
But that jerk...

00:46:23.755 --> 00:46:25.295
Where did that jerk go?

00:46:26.325 --> 00:46:28.495
You can run all you want, but you can't escape Buddha's hand.

00:46:31.065 --> 00:46:32.495
(An Go Eun: Done)

00:46:34.665 --> 00:46:35.665
Alright, all in!

00:46:35.935 --> 00:46:36.935
All in.

00:46:37.675 --> 00:46:39.305
- Jjangttaeng. - Gosh!

00:46:39.845 --> 00:46:43.445
- To beat a Jjangttaeng... - It's a Gwangttaeng.

00:46:43.975 --> 00:46:47.615
Oh dear, what are you going to do now you've lost the company's money?

00:46:47.685 --> 00:46:49.485
Oh, no. All I have is a nine.

00:46:54.785 --> 00:46:56.125
It's a Gwangttaeng!

00:46:57.455 --> 00:46:58.655
Yes, I won! Game over.

00:47:00.065 --> 00:47:02.595
Man, that was the best hand I could get.

00:47:02.625 --> 00:47:04.465
Here, take a taxi home. It's not safe to walk.

00:47:04.795 --> 00:47:06.305
That was fun.

00:47:47.205 --> 00:47:49.975
- Just thinking of it upsets me. - Why?

00:47:50.545 --> 00:47:52.775
- Weren't you up there? - Don't even get me started.

00:47:53.115 --> 00:47:56.415
That guy, the taxi company's CEO, asked to meet, so I went.

00:47:56.885 --> 00:47:59.185
And gosh, he just went on and on about some stupid gukbap.

00:47:59.585 --> 00:48:01.255
I'm telling you, I thought my ears were going to bleed.

00:48:07.265 --> 00:48:08.565
Darn it...

00:48:08.895 --> 00:48:09.895
Weird, right?

00:48:11.665 --> 00:48:14.065
I'm telling you, let's just get rid of them all!

00:48:17.235 --> 00:48:19.205
What are you doing here?

00:48:19.635 --> 00:48:21.805
The guys from the taxi company wouldn't let me leave.

00:48:25.915 --> 00:48:27.585
(Successfully received Premium DB)

00:48:27.645 --> 00:48:29.045
(I'll put it to good use! Thanks, Premium DB!)

00:48:29.115 --> 00:48:30.115
By any chance,

00:48:31.115 --> 00:48:33.925
- did we send them the script? - What script are you talking about?

00:48:34.925 --> 00:48:36.055
The boat's already here,

00:48:36.425 --> 00:48:38.855
so why were you in such a hurry to see me?

00:48:38.995 --> 00:48:40.625
Get in. We can talk on the way.

00:48:40.765 --> 00:48:42.625
Hey, honey.

00:48:42.795 --> 00:48:44.265
Are you done with work?

00:48:44.595 --> 00:48:45.595
Yes.

00:48:50.905 --> 00:48:52.175
Darn it!

00:48:52.975 --> 00:48:56.545
Kim Do Gi... Kim Do Gi, you scum!

00:48:57.215 --> 00:48:59.945
- Darn it! - Darn.

00:49:23.065 --> 00:49:24.705
What is this? All this grass...

00:49:27.075 --> 00:49:30.315
No. What is this? Please... This can't be happening!

00:49:36.585 --> 00:49:38.585
A Na!

00:49:39.555 --> 00:49:42.285
Ana! Are you okay?

00:49:42.685 --> 00:49:43.755
Darn it.

00:49:49.895 --> 00:49:52.965
What's all the commotion? Did something happen?

00:49:55.165 --> 00:49:58.835
- Hey. What's that smoke? - Isn't that the Police Substation?

00:49:58.975 --> 00:50:01.975
Oh, no! Wait, hold on...

00:50:02.505 --> 00:50:03.515
My gosh!

00:50:11.255 --> 00:50:12.255
Hey!

00:50:17.325 --> 00:50:18.525
Your opponent...

00:50:19.725 --> 00:50:20.925
isn't over there, is he?

00:50:38.915 --> 00:50:42.115
"Do no harm." Do not take a life.

00:50:44.915 --> 00:50:47.955
How can you defy Buddha's teachings like that?

00:51:32.165 --> 00:51:34.335
- You okay? - Let's go.

00:51:58.655 --> 00:51:59.655
Darn it.

00:52:04.895 --> 00:52:05.995
Darn it.

00:52:15.875 --> 00:52:19.645
(Server down)

00:53:09.065 --> 00:53:11.665
What's that? Who did that?

00:53:13.365 --> 00:53:15.235
- It wasn't me. - Me neither.

00:53:20.205 --> 00:53:21.205
It was me.

00:53:22.745 --> 00:53:23.915
A Na!

00:53:23.975 --> 00:53:24.975
(Police Station)

00:53:27.285 --> 00:53:28.745
I took care of everything.

00:53:30.655 --> 00:53:33.385
I wasn't sure what else I could do to help.

00:53:34.155 --> 00:53:36.555
- Nice work. - You're the best.

00:53:41.495 --> 00:53:44.365
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:53:44.395 --> 00:53:45.835
What happened with their affiliates?

00:53:45.895 --> 00:53:48.705
They should be pretty much taken care of by now.

00:53:49.165 --> 00:53:52.575
I sent it as a "special DB." They'll probably open it, right?

00:53:53.905 --> 00:53:55.945
Let's get out of here on the boat before those guys notice.

00:53:56.005 --> 00:53:58.515
- Okay. - I think they've already caught on.

00:54:02.885 --> 00:54:04.455
You really got me good.

00:54:05.315 --> 00:54:08.455
It feels good getting a compliment from a former prosecutor.

00:54:10.255 --> 00:54:11.755
You guys doing all this...

00:54:13.295 --> 00:54:15.865
What exactly is in it for you?

00:54:16.625 --> 00:54:19.835
I've been racking my brain, but I just don't get it.

00:54:20.365 --> 00:54:22.565
Why would you go to such lengths?

00:54:23.065 --> 00:54:24.075
Why?

00:54:25.875 --> 00:54:29.175
Why go through all this? Why?

00:54:29.445 --> 00:54:31.675
I'm asking you, why are you doing all this?

00:54:34.545 --> 00:54:35.685
Because I care about them.

00:54:38.255 --> 00:54:40.625
The new mom who's trying to save even a little on baby supplies,

00:54:41.055 --> 00:54:43.955
who spends all day looking through resale apps.

00:54:44.425 --> 00:54:47.195
The eight-year-old buying gloves for her father in the hospital...

00:54:47.395 --> 00:54:51.695
by breaking the piggy bank she'd been saving up for a year.

00:54:52.765 --> 00:54:56.265
And that man who only feels secure when he has 5,000 dollars.

00:55:00.035 --> 00:55:01.275
I care about them a lot.

00:55:08.085 --> 00:55:10.085
Now I see.

00:55:11.885 --> 00:55:16.795
Why people always died or disappeared in your wake.

00:55:20.395 --> 00:55:21.695
But what are you going to do?

00:55:23.965 --> 00:55:24.965
This time,

00:55:27.165 --> 00:55:28.435
that's going to be you.

00:55:38.075 --> 00:55:39.145
Darn it.

00:55:43.655 --> 00:55:44.685
Darn.

00:55:46.385 --> 00:55:47.925
(Samheung Inn)

00:55:59.335 --> 00:56:01.305
I think that siren's for us.

00:56:01.905 --> 00:56:04.505
- Come on, to the docks! Quick! - Right.

00:56:04.735 --> 00:56:07.245
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:56:18.885 --> 00:56:20.425
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:56:24.895 --> 00:56:25.895
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:56:54.885 --> 00:56:55.885
Darn it.

00:56:55.955 --> 00:56:57.395
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:57:15.675 --> 00:57:16.675
Closer!

00:57:20.685 --> 00:57:21.845
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:57:23.245 --> 00:57:24.255
- Darn it. - Gosh.

00:57:33.395 --> 00:57:34.565
Follow them this way.

00:57:39.595 --> 00:57:42.735
I'll lure those guys away. Secure the boat while I do.

00:57:42.805 --> 00:57:44.775
Okay, I'll go on ahead and get the engine started.

00:57:45.205 --> 00:57:46.205
Hurry back.

00:57:48.075 --> 00:57:49.075
Die!

00:57:53.075 --> 00:57:54.785
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:58:00.015 --> 00:58:02.085
Those jerks. They think they can mess with Samheung Island?

00:58:08.365 --> 00:58:09.865
What are you doing? Get after them!

00:58:10.195 --> 00:58:11.935
It's bulletproof glass!

00:58:14.035 --> 00:58:15.065
Hey, go!

00:58:17.235 --> 00:58:20.475
Bulletproof glass? Who are these guys?

00:58:21.005 --> 00:58:24.345
You underestimated Samheung Island!

00:58:32.155 --> 00:58:35.885
- You can't escape this island. - Floor it!

00:58:35.955 --> 00:58:37.225
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:58:39.525 --> 00:58:40.895
There they are.

00:58:41.425 --> 00:58:42.425
Ram them.

00:58:48.265 --> 00:58:51.235
- Unbelievable. Seriously. - Let's run them down!

00:58:51.875 --> 00:58:53.475
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:58:54.605 --> 00:58:56.145
Kill them! Run them off the road!

00:58:57.415 --> 00:58:58.745
Ram them!

00:59:03.785 --> 00:59:04.785
Floor it!

00:59:06.815 --> 00:59:08.955
Push them!

00:59:12.025 --> 00:59:14.125
Come on!

00:59:19.165 --> 00:59:20.805
(Deluxe Taxi)

00:59:32.075 --> 00:59:35.545
- What? We're losing ground! - Hey, die!

00:59:53.495 --> 00:59:55.865
Just ram them all off the road! Harder!

01:00:07.115 --> 01:00:08.315
Floor it!

01:00:10.515 --> 01:00:12.455
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:00:49.555 --> 01:00:51.795
Step on it more!

01:00:52.495 --> 01:00:54.625
Back off!

01:00:55.425 --> 01:00:59.065
Run them off the road. Kill them.

01:00:59.895 --> 01:01:00.965
That's it.

01:01:01.835 --> 01:01:05.235
Die, Kim Do Gi, you jerk! Die!

01:01:11.975 --> 01:01:14.585
- Step on it! - Back off!

01:01:14.645 --> 01:01:15.915
Die!

01:01:48.515 --> 01:01:49.515
Wait a second.

01:01:50.145 --> 01:01:52.915
Why did I build another one of these? Go Eun will kill me.

01:01:55.885 --> 01:01:58.595
But you must have one of these.

01:02:00.325 --> 01:02:03.325
You never know what might happen.

01:02:07.505 --> 01:02:09.135
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:02:09.165 --> 01:02:11.005
If they never have to use it, all the better.

01:02:13.835 --> 01:02:16.575
I should give Driver Kim a heads-up about it.

01:02:25.685 --> 01:02:26.985
(EMP)

01:02:51.575 --> 01:02:52.615
Driver Kim.

01:02:56.985 --> 01:02:57.985
Oh, gosh.

01:03:30.955 --> 01:03:31.985
Do Gi!

01:03:33.685 --> 01:03:34.725
Driver Kim!

01:03:35.985 --> 01:03:37.155
Are you hurt?

01:03:37.525 --> 01:03:39.825
Yes, I'm fine.

01:03:40.095 --> 01:03:41.495
What was all that?

01:03:44.465 --> 01:03:45.465
Could it be...

01:03:50.935 --> 01:03:52.735
What's with all these cars?

01:03:53.175 --> 01:03:57.345
The high-power discharge takes all the electrical power...

01:03:57.415 --> 01:03:58.975
and releases it all at once.

01:03:59.575 --> 01:04:02.385
I guess that's what fried all the other cars.

01:04:03.185 --> 01:04:04.685
The Deluxe Taxi is totaled.

01:04:05.355 --> 01:04:06.355
What did you say?

01:04:07.215 --> 01:04:10.285
- Chief Park, what did you do? - Well...

01:04:10.355 --> 01:04:13.025
What? You did something...

01:04:13.095 --> 01:04:16.065
that turned our taxi into junk just like that? Is that right?

01:04:16.125 --> 01:04:18.195
- No, it's just that... - But thanks to him,

01:04:18.595 --> 01:04:19.735
I'm still alive.

01:04:20.335 --> 01:04:21.335
Thank you,

01:04:21.905 --> 01:04:22.905
Chief Park.

01:04:23.435 --> 01:04:24.435
Really?

01:04:26.075 --> 01:04:27.205
In that case...

01:04:27.845 --> 01:04:29.075
Great job, Chief Park.

01:04:29.975 --> 01:04:32.575
In that case, great job. Good work, Jin Eon.

01:04:32.815 --> 01:04:34.185
Don't you have a mind of your own?

01:04:34.445 --> 01:04:38.285
What does my opinion matter? What matters is what Go Eun thinks.

01:04:38.785 --> 01:04:39.785
What?

01:04:40.585 --> 01:04:42.655
Looks like that boat over there is moving.

01:04:56.135 --> 01:04:57.235
It's Writer Go.

01:05:10.315 --> 01:05:13.015
Hey. You think you've won, don't you?

01:05:13.485 --> 01:05:14.485
Think again.

01:05:15.585 --> 01:05:16.925
All I need is me.

01:05:17.495 --> 01:05:20.895
As long as I'm around, I can rebuild everything.

01:06:08.205 --> 01:06:13.875
(Public Official ID Card, Supreme Prosecutors' Office)

01:06:24.255 --> 01:06:25.825
Hello, this is Reporter Bong.

01:06:25.895 --> 01:06:27.055
(NEWSTART, Live)

01:06:27.125 --> 01:06:29.395
I've been away on assignment.

01:06:31.135 --> 01:06:32.635
He's like a totally different person.

01:06:33.035 --> 01:06:36.735
A ring providing goods and services for criminal acts,

01:06:37.035 --> 01:06:38.935
earning massive profits in the process,

01:06:39.205 --> 01:06:40.575
has finally been taken down.

01:06:40.945 --> 01:06:43.375
This organization, centered around a former prosecutor,

01:06:44.075 --> 01:06:47.375
spawned over a hundred overseas criminal franchises.

01:06:48.215 --> 01:06:51.485
While the major media ignored this and remained silent,

01:06:52.715 --> 01:06:54.185
our team has been covering this case.

01:06:54.885 --> 01:06:57.225
We, the late Shin Kyung Soo investigative journalism team,

01:06:58.625 --> 01:07:00.055
have witnessed firsthand...

01:07:00.865 --> 01:07:03.065
what kind of lawless wasteland is created...

01:07:03.525 --> 01:07:05.495
when a guardian of the law turns their back...

01:07:05.865 --> 01:07:07.765
and abuses the very system they swore to protect.

01:07:08.505 --> 01:07:10.035
You've all been through so much.

01:07:10.535 --> 01:07:13.305
Tonight, premium Korean beef is on me.

01:07:13.875 --> 01:07:14.875
Finally!

01:07:15.245 --> 01:07:17.475
In that case, I'm definitely eating a lot tonight.

01:07:17.675 --> 01:07:20.045
- Okay, let's go to the BBQ place. - Sounds good.

01:07:20.175 --> 01:07:22.245
Wait, we still have to take care of business.

01:07:22.315 --> 01:07:24.185
Take care of what business?

01:07:24.285 --> 01:07:29.225
We have to end our operation before we can go eat. Right, Driver Kim?

01:07:31.255 --> 01:07:34.325
- Like this? - You have to do it by the book.

01:07:36.065 --> 01:07:38.595
But this isn't the Deluxe Taxi, so there's no radio...

01:08:06.755 --> 01:08:08.765
Vehicle 5283 is now ending service.

01:08:09.865 --> 01:08:12.565
- Time for some beef! - Let's go!

01:08:16.865 --> 01:08:19.875
(Deluxe Taxi)

01:08:51.605 --> 01:08:53.175
(We would like to thank Kim Sung Kyu and Lee Kyoung Young.)

01:09:05.685 --> 01:09:08.655
(Deluxe Taxi 3)

01:09:09.155 --> 01:09:12.055
Captain Kim Do Gi. How have you been?

01:09:12.855 --> 01:09:14.565
Gosh, why is his phone off?

01:09:15.225 --> 01:09:18.465
To just abandon his taxi, something serious must've happened.

01:09:18.835 --> 01:09:22.335
It says Sergeant Yoo Seon Ah went AWOL during training.

01:09:22.535 --> 01:09:24.405
She was killed in an explosion while trying to escape.

01:09:24.705 --> 01:09:25.905
It's a military base. I'm sure of it.

01:09:26.205 --> 01:09:29.545
He's getting closer to the Demarcation Line. This is unnerving.

01:09:30.805 --> 01:09:33.215
Something's definitely happened to Driver Kim.

01:09:35.685 --> 01:09:37.715
We have to get to Driver Kim right now.

01:09:37.885 --> 01:09:39.955
Halt. Driver, step out of the vehicle.

01:09:40.015 --> 01:09:42.685
- Identify yourself. - Captain Kim Do Gi.